# std/import-source (design/agent-github.md, "Importing"): an ordinary writer
# (design/tool-contract.md). It holds no token: it imports through its
# neighbour `DEEP-DEPS/github`, the one image the github-token is granted to,
# and answers with its root directory holding the new source tree. Nothing is
# recorded before the import.
HELP=<<END
Import an HTTPS Git repository as a new, unchanged snapshot. Returns its full commit hash; preserves its tree and ancestor history. Does not merge or overwrite code. `root` is the directory it goes in, one per repo, such as sources/<repo> (it may not exist yet); `into` is the new source tree's name there: 00-base, the upstream tip the stack builds on, which is never edited, so `copy` it to 99-dirty to work (see std/GIT.md). Public repositories need no token. The remote is observed when the call runs, so to see a branch's CURRENT head call this again with a fresh `into`, such as 00-base-2: the new snapshot is how you learn the hash, and the tree you merge from. Its provenance is written beside it as <into>.source.json. Do not do this to update a stack: caos-std/stack-sync reads and imports the trunk's head and every layer's branch itself, so run it directly, without importing first.
@param source HTTPS repository URL, without credentials.
@param [revision] Remote branch, full refs/... name, or full commit hash. Omit for the remote default branch.
@param into Unused name inside root for the new source tree, such as 00-base, or 00-base-2 for a newer tip outside a stack. Its .source.json sibling must also be free.
@writer
@root
@request-id
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/go --worker1:@=worker.go --github:@=DEEP-DEPS/github --help=$HELP
